'''Amit Kumar''' (born 3 July 1952) is an Indian [[playback singer]], [[music composer]] and [[actor]]. Kumar launched his own music production company, named Kumar Brothers Music. He has predominantly worked in  [[Bollywood]] and regional film songs since the 1970s, including 150 Hindi and Bengali compositions by [[R. D. Burman]] and [[Bappi Lahiri]]. After Burman's death in 1994, citing a lack of quality music composition, Kumar withdrew from playback singing and concentrated on live orchestra shows. In addition to singing in Hindi, has also performed in [[Bengali language|Bengali]], [[Bhojpuri language|Bhojpuri]], [[Odia language|Odia]], [[Assamese language|Assamese]], [[Marathi language|Marathi]] and [[Konkani language|Konkani]]. He is the eldest son of singer-actor [[Kishore Kumar]].<ref name="auto">{{Cite web |title=Legendary Kishore Kumar's son Amit Kumar talks about his father |url=https://www.filmfare.com/features/legendary-kishore-kumars-son-amit-kumar-talks-about-his-father-27659.html |access-date=17 December 2020 |website=filmfare.com |language=en}}</ref><ref name="Amit Kumar's special tribute"/>

